From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 17:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: complete WCN3990 and enable MPSS

The first WCN3990 hardware probe binds ath10k_snoc and the Apps SMMU stream,
but reports the fifth WLAN rail as missing and never receives the WLFW QMI
service while MPSS is disabled.

Describe the remaining 3.3 V channel and start MPSS with the firmware path
provided by firmware-oneplus-hotdog-modem. Keep the validated low-memory RMTFS
layout unchanged.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -231,7 +231,8 @@
 };
 
 &remoteproc_mpss {
-	status = "disabled";
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/modem.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &wifi {
@@ -242,6 +243,7 @@
 	vdd-1.8-xo-supply = <&vreg_l7a_1p8>;
 	vdd-1.3-rfa-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p3>;
 	vdd-3.3-ch0-supply = <&vreg_l11c_3p3>;
+	vdd-3.3-ch1-supply = <&vreg_l10c_3p3>;
 };
 
 &rmtfs_mem {
-- 
2.50.1
